        "excerpt": "An income building without an inspection certificate can still be traded, but you need to check its legal compliance (conformity with the Building Standards Act) before acquiring. The certificate is proof of passing the completion inspection (Building Standards Act Art. 7); its absence does not itself mean illegality. Existing-nonconforming (Art. 3(2)) is lawful; a code-violating building is not. Written by a licensed real estate agent and administrative scrivener in Bunkyo, Tokyo.",
